{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nexp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"981f67969ef44bc1b4d8e296cbb610c4-question-1\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_resurrect_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"cff2222705354f669ca24cef6629804a-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"Adds a third case to the same scenario that pins the trigger boundary: in the shallow case the two commits that push the persisted commit index past the removal entry are omitted, so the removal entry stays above the replayed prefix. Existing cases, observations and comparisons are unchanged; one comparison is added for the shallow case, where the committed membership must be kept.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\",\\\"vote_prevote_checks\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Same four-phase scenario as the executed revision (A and B bootstrapped, A snapshots, C shut down for its own removal, RemoveServer C committed, then either two further commits or none depending on the case, A restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs or without it, C brought back and caught up, B partitioned, one Apply on the leader), with a third case restore_on_shallow that omits the two extra commits. The probe records the staged commit index before each restart and the resulting configuration, peer count and write outcome in every case.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The staged commit index only advances when a log entry is dispatched, so omitting the extra commits leaves it below the removal entry's index; the observation records the staged value (5 in the shallow case against 7 in the failing case) so the difference is inspectable.\\\",\\\"The shallow case is otherwise identical in operations, stores and transports, so the only difference is whether the removal entry falls inside the replayed prefix.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No control is added for the shallow case beyond comparing it with the failing case and the flag-off case, which already exist in the same execution.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"peers\\\":3,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":50}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap, real snapshot, real shutdown of C, real RemoveServer, real commits (two, or none in the shallow case), real restart of A on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore instances, real restart of C, real partition. No fabricated state; the shallow case only omits ordinary client commits.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"before_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"before_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_setup_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_is_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_setup_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_is_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_shallow\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"before_restart_restore_on_shallow\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on_shallow\\\"}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A restarted leader must not count a voter whose removal is committed in its own log (failing case).\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the same restart without RestoreCommittedLogs keeps the committed membership.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_write_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"entry_on_quorum\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A write whose Apply reported success must be held by a quorum of the configuration committed in the log.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_write_restore_off\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_write_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"write_applied\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with the committed membership the same partition must make the leader refuse the write.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_restart_restore_on_shallow\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_res_shallow\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Boundary: with the removal entry above the replayed prefix the restart must keep the committed membership and must not resurrect the removed voter.\\\"}\n ]\n}\nd['experiment']=exp\npar=d['interpretations'][0]\npar['limitations'].append(\\\"The trigger boundary is being executed in both directions: a construction-time run of the extended resurrect harness kept the committed membership when the removal entry stayed above the replayed prefix (staged commit 5 against removal entry index 7: two servers, no removed voter, peers 1, and the partitioned write refused), while the same harness with the two extra commits reproduced the resurrection and the accepted write. Its retained receipt is requested in this update; if it holds, the condition 'at or below the persisted commit index' in the summary is confirmed by execution rather than by reasoning alone.\\\")\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
